    "B1": "Missed by 0.009 (0.741 vs 0.750 threshold), far inside the replicate spread of +/-0.113. Reported as FAILED as pre-registered. Resolving a margin this small requires more data, not a moved threshold: re-run on longer trajectories (ATLAS/mdCATH) with the SAME 0.75 bar.",
    "B3": "Failed only because rarity_only = 0.611 exceeded the 0.60 band. DIAGNOSIS: rarity was mis-classified as time-blind when the criteria were written. rarity = 1 - pi, and pi is estimated by the reversible MLE from the TRANSITION COUNT MATRIX, so it inherits temporal information from the frame ordering. It is semi-kinetic, not time-blind. Every genuinely time-blind detector is inside the band: rmsd_from_mean 0.536, feature_zscore 0.513, isolation_forest 0.471, local_outlier_factor 0.546, density_only 0.530. This is recorded as a flaw in the pre-registration, NOT silently corrected - a corrected replication must be run and reported separately.",
    "what_is_established": "B2 and B4 passed decisively. The null control sits at 0.501, confirming the construction is sound, and the naive frame-to-frame jump detector sits at exactly 0.500 in near mode, confirming the junctions are geometrically invisible by design. Against that, transition surprise reaches 0.741 - the only method meaningfully above chance. This supports the claim that the kinetic channel detects transitions no geometric detector can see, at a confidence level short of the pre-registered bar."
